13K Control is an independent, unofficial macOS controller for DASUNG
Paperlike 13K monitors. The application is original Swift source.

It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by DASUNG / 大上科技.
“DASUNG”, “Paperlike”, and “13K” are used only to identify the hardware
this software can talk to.

The USB-serial framing (24-character uppercase ASCII hex packets starting
with 5FF5 and ending with A0FA, CH340 1a86:7523 at 115200 8N1) is the
device’s own control protocol. This project implements that protocol for
interoperability and does not redistribute vendor binaries, assets, or
source.

GPU dithering uses public IOMobileFramebuffer properties (`enableDither`,
`uniformity2D`).
